+    /**
+     * Charge a spell cast in our own main phase for the lands it taps only when those lands were
+     * holding up an instant-speed card — [permanentCastIsNotCardLoss]'s argument, applied to the
+     * mana instead of the card.
+     *
+     * `BoardPresence` prices an untapped land 0.6 and a tapped one 0.3, flat. Without
+     * [sequenceLandsByUsableMana] that is the whole cost of spending mana, and it is a real cost in
+     * one situation only: a land tapped now is not untapped on the opponent's turn, so an instant or
+     * flash card in hand loses its window. With nothing like that in hand, mana not spent in our own
+     * main phase is simply lost at end of turn, but the charge (0.45 per land at the default weight)
+     * still applies. A two-mana rock is worth 0.75 to the evaluator without card knowledge, so it is
+     * worth less than the two lands it taps, and so is every other cheap non-creature permanent.
+     * Off a 2026-11-02 Eldrazi Incursion mirror (`EldraziIncursionPlayableTest`, seed 1), both seats
+     * passed every main phase from turn 10 to 30 with two Talismans, Herald's Horn and Garruk's
+     * Uprising castable, each scored 0.25–1.0 below passing, and the game hit its turn cap.
+     *
+     * `Strategist` therefore refunds exactly the land charge the evaluator applied:
+     * `evaluate(leaf with the spent lands untapped) − evaluate(leaf)`. It does so only for a cast from
+     * our own main phase with the stack empty, and only if the lands left untapped can still cast
+     * every instant-speed card in hand that the root's untapped lands could cast. An instant we could
+     * not have afforded anyway (mana value above the untapped land count) does not hold mana. Like
+     * `BoardPresence`'s idle-mana term, this compares mana value with a land count and ignores colours;
+     * a mana solver call per candidate is not affordable here. A tap that breaks the instant's window
+     * is charged as before, so a held answer still keeps its mana.
+     */
+    val manaHeldOnlyForInstants: Boolean = false,
     /**
      * Score `ThreatAssessment`'s evasion term the way it reads after an attack, so attacking with a
      * flier the opponent cannot block stops reading as a loss.
